# Security response headers (OWASP A05: Security Misconfiguration).
# Honored by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages; copied verbatim into dist/ at build time.
# Content-Security-Policy is emitted separately as a per-page <meta> element by Astro
# (security.csp in astro.config.mjs), so it is intentionally NOT duplicated here to avoid
# two conflicting policies. The headers below are the ones a <meta> tag cannot deliver.
#
# Hosts that do not read _headers:
#   - Vercel: use vercel.json "headers" (see docs/security/).
#   - GitHub Pages: cannot set custom headers; the <meta> CSP still applies, but nosniff,
#     HSTS, X-Frame-Options, and Permissions-Policy will be absent. Prefer a host that
#     supports custom headers for full coverage.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), browsing-topics=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
